*.tsbuildinfo

# Git worktrees (superpowers subagent-driven-development isolation)
.worktrees/

# Session working files — seed undo manifests, generator scripts, scratch data.
# Never deliverables, and seeded-log-ids.json is the only way to clean up a
# seeded account, so it must not be shared or overwritten via git.
scratchpad/

# Deno lockfile for the edge functions — deliberately NOT committed.
# `supabase functions deploy` does not use it: the deployed runtime resolves the
# specifiers itself. Locking CI would therefore make CI green against versions
# prod is not running, so the type-check would stop being an early warning that
# an upstream release breaks a live function.
#
# An earlier version of this note said to commit the lock once the specifiers
# were pinned. They now are (2026-09-08) and the note was wrong: exact pins close
# the DIRECT dependency gap, but supabase-js and the Anthropic SDK still resolve
# their own transitive deps by range at deploy time. The same argument applies
# one level down, so the lock stays out.
supabase/functions/deno.lock
